      "widgets_values": [
        "A single continuous five-second cinematic shot, photorealistic. An isolated, weathered white lighthouse stands upright on dark wet coastal rocks at the centre of the frame, its warm amber lantern glowing against a stormy slate-blue sea and overcast sky. From the first frame, a large swell is already rolling in just left of centre; its slate-blue face rises, the crest curls over and slams into the rocks at the lighthouse base, bursting into a broad white plume of spray that rises beside the tower and drifts in the wind, then collapses into foaming runoff streaming back down the rock faces. The camera advances smoothly toward the lighthouse with a gentle arc to the right, revealing clear parallax between foreground rocks, the breaking wave and the steady tower. The lighthouse stays rigid, vertical and unchanged, with tower and wave held together at the heart of the composition. Physically plausible water, mist, moody natural light. No people, no text, no logos.",
